WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:50.806
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:51.076 --> 00:52.873
I'm throwing you, okay?

3
01:08.696 --> 01:10.719
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

4
01:12.135 --> 01:14.419
I did it, right?

5
01:15.649 --> 01:17.266
Right?

6
01:22.441 --> 01:24.675
Oh my Gosh!

7
01:24.675 --> 01:26.703
What is this?

8
01:32.628 --> 01:34.383
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

9
01:35.341 --> 01:36.889
Get up.

10
01:37.635 --> 01:39.364
Hurry, get up.

11
01:46.716 --> 01:48.549
Yoon Ha Na?

12
01:57.759 --> 01:59.693
Let's do it one more time.

13
02:11.911 --> 02:17.154
Why did they call Dangun Wanggeom of Gojoseon the king of theocracy?

14
02:18.589 --> 02:21.099
Hey, what's with the attitude?

15
02:22.652 --> 02:24.649
He didn't only have a hand in politics,

16
02:24.649 --> 02:26.749
- but took part in rituals... - When we go back,

17
02:26.749 --> 02:28.871
we get Woo Jae back into sports.

18
02:28.871 --> 02:30.569
What will you do?

19
02:30.569 --> 02:33.266
I'll be the one in your body, not you.

20
02:33.266 --> 02:34.679
Don't worry about it.

21
02:34.679 --> 02:36.275
Yoon Ha Ru's body?

22
02:36.275 --> 02:39.696
It's already been perfected by senior year.

23
02:40.973 --> 02:43.395
- In the roots of our history... - I wonder if Yoon Ha Na is doing okay?

24
02:43.395 --> 02:45.699
there were communicators of the unseen world...

25
02:49.897 --> 02:51.289
Yoon Ha Ru!

26
02:51.289 --> 02:53.489
Faster!

27
02:54.738 --> 02:56.191
Come on!

28
02:56.865 --> 02:58.972
It's too heavy!

29
03:03.885 --> 03:06.465
We'll start over if I catch you!

30
03:07.326 --> 03:08.826
Come on!

31
03:09.484 --> 03:11.204
Faster, faster!

32
03:11.204 --> 03:13.567
Perfected? What a liar!

33
03:26.691 --> 03:28.155
I don't like this at all.

34
03:28.155 --> 03:29.439
That's not how you do it.

35
03:29.439 --> 03:30.678
You need to use sudden force!

36
03:30.678 --> 03:32.162
Sudden, get it?

37
03:32.162 --> 03:33.626
Yoon Ha Ru.

38
03:33.626 --> 03:35.901
Flip your opponent over like this.

39
03:35.901 --> 03:37.131
Sudden force, see.

40
03:37.131 --> 03:38.848
This is how you do it.

41
03:38.848 --> 03:40.992
Give it some more oomph.

42
03:40.992 --> 03:43.663
Were you starved as a kid? Why are you so weak?

43
03:46.797 --> 03:49.228
The sun's going to set at this rate!

44
03:49.228 --> 03:50.930
Hurry, let's wrap this up.

45
03:50.930 --> 03:52.260
Get up, come on!

46
03:52.260 --> 03:54.085
- Let's go. - We're almost there, come on!

47
03:54.085 --> 03:55.585
Let's go!

48
04:20.349 --> 04:21.849
Thanks.

49
04:30.709 --> 04:32.976
- They believed in the power of nature - Jung Woo Jae...

50
04:32.976 --> 04:35.235
- and prayed for communal prosperity - starts judo again...

51
04:35.235 --> 04:37.778
- via rituals. - made it into the national team...

52
04:37.778 --> 04:38.918
That is why the leader of that era...

53
04:38.918 --> 04:41.524
- Okay, that's done. - was not only a king of the people...

54
04:41.524 --> 04:43.853
but a bridge between the gods and humans.

55
04:43.853 --> 04:46.072
Like a shaman.

56
04:46.817 --> 04:48.935
Can I really trust Yoon Ha Na?

57
04:48.935 --> 04:51.003
- I hope she doesn't screw up. - When the soul leaves the body,

58
04:51.003 --> 04:54.604
they believed the body to be an empty husk.

59
04:55.573 --> 04:59.761
So, if the husk got taken over by a stray soul...

60
04:59.761 --> 05:01.484
or got lost,

61
05:01.484 --> 05:03.406
what did they do?

62
05:08.163 --> 05:12.308
[Shaman] Back then, to them, shamans and rituals...

63
05:12.308 --> 05:14.229
were like the doctors of the present times.

64
05:14.229 --> 05:15.230
It was healing.

65
05:15.230 --> 05:17.577
They believed shamans to be pathfinders for spirits.

66
05:17.577 --> 05:19.358
A spiritual guide, so to speak.

67
05:19.358 --> 05:21.014
Sir!

68
05:21.014 --> 05:22.566
What is it, Yoon Ha Na?

69
05:22.566 --> 05:24.304
It's rare that you have a question.

70
05:24.304 --> 05:26.168
That "spiritual guide" stuff...

71
05:26.168 --> 05:28.747
Do you think it could still fly in our present day?

72
05:28.747 --> 05:30.940
Well, historically speaking...

73
05:30.940 --> 05:32.608
the form may have changed,

74
05:32.608 --> 05:35.355
but the idea of spirituality still exists, yes.

75
05:35.355 --> 05:38.148
It's a cultural tradition, you see.

76
05:39.743 --> 05:40.965
Why?

77
05:40.965 --> 05:43.585
Do you want to know the future? Thinking of going to a fortune teller?

78
05:44.255 --> 05:46.461
No, nothing like that.

79
05:46.461 --> 05:49.967
Well, just the fact that Yoon Ha Na is awake during class...

80
05:49.967 --> 05:52.910
- is enough to make me happy. - A spiritual guide...

81
05:52.910 --> 05:54.626
Now, another point to be mindful of...

82
05:54.626 --> 05:56.474
- Not bad. - Can anyone tell me what it is?

83
05:56.474 --> 05:57.875
The seasonal rituals of the Three Hans.

84
05:57.875 --> 05:59.413
- A spiritual... - Every December,

85
05:59.413 --> 06:00.507
- guide... - there was a ritual called Yeonggo.

86
06:00.507 --> 06:02.301
Which nation was that?

87
06:07.179 --> 06:09.379
All done.

88
06:15.482 --> 06:17.927
It'll get better soon, I guess.

89
06:20.117 --> 06:21.118
Can't you knock?

90
06:21.118 --> 06:22.491
Who cares if I saw?

91
06:22.491 --> 06:24.731
It's my body, anyway.

92
06:24.731 --> 06:27.956
It's just a sore muscle, no need for all that.

93
06:27.956 --> 06:30.040
What a weakling.

94
06:30.670 --> 06:31.671
What do you want?

95
06:31.671 --> 06:34.723
Yeah, we need to have an emergency meeting.

96
06:36.025 --> 06:38.206
Are you certain?

97
06:38.206 --> 06:39.207
Of what?

98
06:39.207 --> 06:41.873
The trials. Are you?

99
06:42.498 --> 06:44.425
I'm doing my best.

100
06:44.425 --> 06:45.648
That's not enough.

101
06:45.648 --> 06:49.447
My body may be a gift from the skies above,

102
06:49.447 --> 06:54.471
but you lack the software to make use of the top-tier hardware.

103
06:55.192 --> 06:57.228
Top-tier? You've got to be kidding me.

104
06:57.228 --> 06:58.551
Well? Any good ideas?

105
06:58.551 --> 07:01.856
Personal training. Starting today.

106
07:01.856 --> 07:03.793
Personal training?

107
07:23.075 --> 07:24.688
Check back into the dorms starting tomorrow.

108
07:24.688 --> 07:27.294
Good job, and good luck.

109
07:50.730 --> 07:52.278
See, judo is all about aura.

110
07:52.278 --> 07:55.969
Once you get a grip, you use your "you're dead meat" stare.

111
07:55.969 --> 07:57.537
Like so.

112
08:06.719 --> 08:08.880
Hey, it's late now.

113
08:08.880 --> 08:11.331
You'll wake up all our neighbors.

114
08:12.039 --> 08:16.481
The ferocity of a judo player knows no rest, day or night! It's on 24/7!

115
08:16.481 --> 08:18.626
Yeah, yeah, sure.

116
08:18.626 --> 08:20.308
Where are your eyes? I said look here!

117
08:20.308 --> 08:22.486
You need to win the staring contest first, okay?

118
08:22.486 --> 08:24.437
See the fire in my eyes, huh?

119
08:24.437 --> 08:26.328
Beat me, come on!

120
08:28.614 --> 08:31.597
I don't know about the fire...

121
08:31.597 --> 08:33.450
but I see your eye boogers.

122
08:33.450 --> 08:34.837
Ugh, seriously!

123
08:34.837 --> 08:38.477
My fierceness, resilience and my toughness...

124
08:38.477 --> 08:40.321
are nowhere to be found.

125
08:40.321 --> 08:45.310
Is this truly the end of my life as a judo player?

126
08:49.877 --> 08:52.351
Why is he texting me instead of just coming in?

127
08:52.351 --> 08:54.567
- Woo Jae? - Yeah.

128
08:54.567 --> 08:55.767
Huh?

129
08:55.767 --> 08:59.069
Why is he asking me to go see a movie?

130
08:59.747 --> 09:01.530
A movie?

131
09:01.530 --> 09:03.385
Ha Na, do you have time tomorrow?

132
09:03.385 --> 09:04.867
Do you want to go see a movie with me?

133
09:04.867 --> 09:07.186
So, what's happening right now is...

134
09:07.186 --> 09:08.547
he's not asking me...

135
09:08.547 --> 09:10.867
but you, right?

136
09:10.867 --> 09:13.542
Well, I think so.

137
09:54.747 --> 09:57.496
Okay! Can Yoon Ha Ru come, too?

138
09:57.496 --> 09:58.870
By the way, why not come inside?

139
09:58.870 --> 10:01.305
Why is he getting in the way?

140
10:02.337 --> 10:04.292
This is not going well.

141
10:11.306 --> 10:12.413
Wait, no.

142
10:12.413 --> 10:14.877
This is my chance to make things clear.

143
10:22.951 --> 10:24.883
Alright, the three of us it is, then.

144
10:24.883 --> 10:26.530
I'm heading in now.

145
10:31.546 --> 10:33.527
[Banana milk]

146
10:33.527 --> 10:35.510
It's Yoon Ha Na.

147
10:35.510 --> 10:38.023
The one I really like is...

148
10:38.023 --> 10:39.616
Yoon Ha Na.

149
10:40.593 --> 10:42.780
Yoon Ha Na, Yoon Ha Na...

150
10:42.780 --> 10:44.337
Yoon Ha Na.

151
10:50.150 --> 10:52.037
What's taking Ha Ru so long?

152
10:52.037 --> 10:54.012
What a pain in my foot.

153
10:57.512 --> 10:59.108
Let's go.

154
11:01.284 --> 11:05.389
You... can't be serious about going out like this.

155
11:05.389 --> 11:06.704
I am.

156
11:06.704 --> 11:08.436
What's wrong?

157
11:09.535 --> 11:10.536
Get inside.

158
11:10.536 --> 11:11.537
Where?

159
11:11.537 --> 11:13.027
Your room, come on! Hurry!

160
11:13.027 --> 11:14.056
- Go inside. - What, why?

161
11:14.056 --> 11:15.582
- Inside, now. - Why?

162
11:17.787 --> 11:19.464
Stand up straight.

163
11:19.464 --> 11:21.285
You want me to wear this?

164
11:21.285 --> 11:23.317
Shut it.

165
11:27.773 --> 11:29.945
This seems to fit nicely.

166
11:29.945 --> 11:31.755
I'm not wearing a dress!

167
11:31.755 --> 11:33.293
Hey!

168
11:34.180 --> 11:35.989
Stay still.

169
11:54.243 --> 11:55.624
Come here.

170
12:00.702 --> 12:02.450
Ugh, you...

171
12:02.450 --> 12:04.135
I said, come here.

172
12:07.784 --> 12:10.311
- All done. - It's over, right?

173
12:13.152 --> 12:14.366
Sit down.

174
12:14.366 --> 12:15.450
Why?

175
12:15.450 --> 12:16.905
I said, sit!

176
12:16.905 --> 12:18.730
Why?

177
12:20.050 --> 12:21.731
You're not leaving like that.

178
12:34.623 --> 12:36.123
Over here.

179
12:51.944 --> 12:53.650
Damn it.

180
12:55.083 --> 12:57.613
What is wrong with him?

181
12:57.613 --> 12:59.003
Where's Jung Woo Jae?

182
12:59.003 --> 13:00.796
He's right outside.

183
13:00.796 --> 13:02.453
Do you have to walk like that?

184
13:02.453 --> 13:04.606
Just be normal for once. Please?

185
13:04.606 --> 13:06.355
I'm begging you.

186
13:06.355 --> 13:08.196
No, hear this.

187
13:08.927 --> 13:10.627
Something's off.

188
13:10.627 --> 13:12.337
Off?

189
13:12.337 --> 13:14.691
I'm constantly feeling this gentle breeze down there.

190
13:14.691 --> 13:17.069
It's like something's missing.

191
13:17.069 --> 13:18.952
It's unsettling.

192
13:20.004 --> 13:22.416
Can you please keep your legs together?

193
13:22.416 --> 13:24.453
I should sue you for defamation!

194
13:24.453 --> 13:26.917
Ugh, alright, alright.

195
13:33.053 --> 13:34.653
Oh, Jung Woo Jae!

196
13:45.852 --> 13:48.367
What took you so long?

197
13:48.367 --> 13:50.040
I was at the convenience store.

198
13:53.449 --> 13:55.763
Let's go inside, Woo Jae.

199
13:55.763 --> 13:57.989
Uh, okay.

200
14:09.299 --> 14:10.636
Ha Na.

201
14:10.636 --> 14:11.846
Have this.

202
14:11.846 --> 14:14.682
Milk? At the movies?

203
14:14.682 --> 14:17.056
Is this why you were late?

204
14:17.056 --> 14:20.418
Yeah, I noticed that you drink this a lot.

205
14:20.418 --> 14:21.956
Coke is the best for watching movies.

206
14:21.956 --> 14:24.231
We're not kids, who's drinking milk?

207
14:27.009 --> 14:28.549
I guess so...

208
14:29.344 --> 14:30.909
I'll drink it.

209
14:32.870 --> 14:34.584
That banana milk...

210
14:34.584 --> 14:35.705
I want it.

211
14:35.705 --> 14:37.205
Give it to me.

212
14:40.056 --> 14:41.676
Okay.

213
15:09.339 --> 15:11.759
That's so funny.

214
15:24.731 --> 15:26.973
So hilarious.

215
15:32.454 --> 15:33.996
Thanks.

216
16:06.905 --> 16:09.543
Private Yoon Ha Ru, reporting for duty!

217
16:14.246 --> 16:15.372
What is wrong with you? Sit down!

218
16:15.372 --> 16:16.884
Sorry.

219
16:26.298 --> 16:29.771
God, I hate him so much!

220
16:39.354 --> 16:44.985
♪ I'll wait through countless mishaps ♪

221
16:44.985 --> 16:50.741
♪ I'll smile through all the pain ♪

222
16:50.741 --> 17:01.208
♪ Don't leave, don't give up yet ♪

223
17:01.208 --> 17:07.509
♪ See this love grow deeper the more you push me away ♪

224
17:07.509 --> 17:13.034
♪ You can hold my tongue, but the world will still know ♪

225
17:13.034 --> 17:15.580
♪ So why are you the only one clueless? ♪

226
17:15.580 --> 17:22.125
♪ Why don't you see the man who will keep you safe? ♪

227
17:26.155 --> 17:29.744
- I ate that up! - Practice harder and try for a perfect score!

228
17:34.818 --> 17:36.269
♪ You ♪

229
17:36.269 --> 17:39.373
♪ When I fall down ♪

230
17:39.373 --> 17:44.455
♪ Don't waver, help me up time and time again ♪

231
17:44.455 --> 17:47.923
♪ With your strong gaze ♪

232
17:47.923 --> 17:49.716
♪ And you ♪

233
17:49.716 --> 17:53.011
♪ When I'm having a hard time ♪

234
17:53.011 --> 17:56.115
♪ You came for me to the edge of the cliff ♪

235
17:56.115 --> 17:57.849
♪ Without fail ♪

236
17:57.849 --> 18:01.849
♪ And held my two hands in yours ♪

237
18:01.849 --> 18:06.360
♪ Though I have nothing to offer ♪

238
18:06.360 --> 18:08.938
♪ Nothing to show ♪

239
18:08.938 --> 18:11.617
♪ But today, for you ♪

240
18:11.617 --> 18:15.075
♪ I sing this song ♪

241
18:15.075 --> 18:16.539
♪ Tonight ♪

242
18:16.539 --> 18:20.170
♪ In your two eyes ♪

243
18:20.170 --> 18:22.603
Take a break, Ha Na.

244
18:22.603 --> 18:23.604
Like you did?

245
18:23.604 --> 18:25.923
Like when you gave up judo?

246
18:25.923 --> 18:28.920
But what do you get after running away?

247
18:28.920 --> 18:31.269
You ended up a bodyguard.

248
18:33.693 --> 18:34.717
Don't be scared.

249
18:34.717 --> 18:36.877
Just be yourself.

250
18:36.877 --> 18:38.988
To me, no one shines brighter...

251
18:38.988 --> 18:41.194
than you, Yoon Ha Na.

252
18:42.109 --> 18:43.795
Thank goodness...

253
18:43.795 --> 18:44.796
Woo Jae!

254
18:44.796 --> 18:46.648
No, wait!

255
18:47.421 --> 18:48.859
What do I do?

256
18:48.859 --> 18:51.838
♪ Never say goodbye ♪

257
18:51.838 --> 18:53.910
♪ Because this world, to me ♪

258
18:53.910 --> 18:57.365
♪ is only you and I ♪

259
19:43.537 --> 19:45.694
Oh, my throat hurts. I'm going to the convenience store.

260
19:45.694 --> 19:46.970
Are you guys going?

261
19:47.582 --> 19:49.011
I'm good.

262
19:49.011 --> 19:50.874
We'll wait for you.

263
20:07.380 --> 20:09.722
Hey. Why the long face?

264
20:10.462 --> 20:11.962
No reason.

265
20:12.705 --> 20:14.909
Just thinking about someone.

266
20:16.003 --> 20:17.343
Who?

267
20:17.983 --> 20:20.001
Just someone.

268
20:20.001 --> 20:21.897
Not the sharpest tool in the shed.

269
20:22.782 --> 20:24.757
Well, who is it?

270
20:31.336 --> 20:33.949
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru.

271
21:09.048 --> 21:10.576
What are you guys doing?

272
21:13.264 --> 21:16.033
It was buy two, get one. Big bro is buying! Want one?

273
21:16.033 --> 21:18.126
Oh, I'm good.

274
21:18.126 --> 21:19.530
Want it?

275
21:31.165 --> 21:32.814
I must be out of my mind.

276
21:32.814 --> 21:34.608
What is wrong with me?

277
21:34.608 --> 21:36.736
Get it together, Jung Woo Jae.

278
21:40.142 --> 21:42.308
The person I like is...

279
21:43.494 --> 21:45.049
Yoon Ha Na.

280
21:46.453 --> 21:47.871
You know...

281
21:47.871 --> 21:49.275
Yeah?

282
21:50.207 --> 21:52.915
I... actually, I...

283
21:54.196 --> 21:56.221
Yeah, what is it? Spit it out.

284
22:00.217 --> 22:02.201
I like you!

285
22:04.523 --> 22:05.889
Huh?

286
22:05.889 --> 22:07.411
What?

287
22:09.369 --> 22:10.737
I...

288
22:11.475 --> 22:13.975
I like you.

289
22:28.328 --> 22:31.125
Jung Woo Jae, you idiot...

290
22:33.010 --> 22:35.258
How is that a proper confession?

291
22:35.258 --> 22:36.866
In what world was that a good idea?

292
22:36.866 --> 22:39.054
Why did I do that in front of a convenience store?

293
22:41.452 --> 22:43.078
Yoon Ha Na.

294
22:43.796 --> 22:46.169
I... actually, I...

295
22:47.597 --> 22:50.157
I like you!

296
22:51.243 --> 22:52.352
Huh?

297
22:52.352 --> 22:53.740
What?

298
23:06.658 --> 23:09.295
Why did it have to be then?

299
23:09.295 --> 23:10.646
Why right then?

300
23:10.646 --> 23:13.414
Why?

301
23:14.970 --> 23:17.657
Oh, man, what do I do?

302
23:17.657 --> 23:21.189
Wow, he just confessed to me!

303
23:21.189 --> 23:22.823
He did it to me, not you.

304
23:22.823 --> 23:24.940
Well, it's me now!

305
23:24.940 --> 23:26.831
Think about it, what if he tried to, like,

306
23:26.831 --> 23:28.876
kiss me, or something?

307
23:28.876 --> 23:30.809
Oh, I'm about to throw up.

308
23:30.809 --> 23:33.459
God, can you stay still for a minute?

309
23:33.459 --> 23:34.762
You saw it too, didn't you?

310
23:34.762 --> 23:36.291
You saw the way he looked at me, right?

311
23:36.291 --> 23:39.486
It was so intense, I thought I'd melt!

312
23:39.486 --> 23:42.805
It's not just my problem, though. How would you feel?

313
23:42.805 --> 23:45.648
Imagine him and me holding hands...

314
23:45.648 --> 23:46.930
and hugging...

315
23:46.930 --> 23:48.717
- and kissing... - Stop!

316
23:50.661 --> 23:52.420
Oh, seriously.

317
23:53.433 --> 23:56.875
Shamans and rituals were like the doctors of the present times.

318
23:56.875 --> 23:57.876
It was healing.

319
23:57.876 --> 24:00.212
They believed shamans to be pathfinders for spirits.

320
24:00.212 --> 24:02.538
A spiritual guide, so to speak.

321
24:02.538 --> 24:05.409
Hey, let's switch.

322
24:05.409 --> 24:07.949
- What? - Our bodies.

323
24:07.949 --> 24:09.448
So, go back to the future?

324
24:09.448 --> 24:10.499
We can't, not yet.

325
24:10.499 --> 24:12.753
We need to see Woo Jae make the national team.

326
24:12.753 --> 24:14.104
No, right now.

327
24:14.104 --> 24:16.422
Let's swap right here, right now.

328
24:16.422 --> 24:19.188
- Huh? - Well, we haven't tried anything.

329
24:19.188 --> 24:20.768
That's because that doesn't make sense!

330
24:20.768 --> 24:22.929
Well, does this right now make sense to you?

331
24:22.929 --> 24:25.126
We've already been swapped, there's no logic to this!

332
24:25.126 --> 24:27.335
It makes no sense!

333
24:27.335 --> 24:29.878
- Well, yeah, I guess so. - Let's try it.

334
24:29.878 --> 24:32.166
I'm desperate, please!

335
24:32.953 --> 24:36.590
Are you seriously worried that he might kiss you?

336
24:39.459 --> 24:41.388
It's about judo.

337
24:42.265 --> 24:43.266
Huh?

338
24:43.266 --> 24:44.995
The trials!

339
24:44.995 --> 24:47.318
There's not much time left.

340
24:48.857 --> 24:51.233
He's obviously going to make it in.

341
24:51.233 --> 24:52.805
But, well...

342
24:52.805 --> 24:54.997
I need to at least come in 2nd place.

343
24:57.486 --> 24:59.105
Yoon Ha Ru...

344
24:59.105 --> 25:01.742
You were really worried.

345
25:02.439 --> 25:04.879
I shouldn't be pressuring you as your big brother.

346
25:04.879 --> 25:06.998
Sorry about that.

347
25:06.998 --> 25:08.173
No.

348
25:08.173 --> 25:09.702
Let's try.

349
25:10.412 --> 25:12.181
The sooner, the better.

350
25:12.181 --> 25:13.474
Okay.

351
25:14.763 --> 25:16.276
So...

352
25:16.875 --> 25:19.151
How are we doing this?

353
25:21.324 --> 25:22.699
Shamanism.

354
25:22.699 --> 25:24.716
Shamanism?

355
25:54.822 --> 25:56.642
Sis!

356
25:56.642 --> 25:59.144
You're standing on the edge of a cliff, sis.

357
25:59.144 --> 26:02.854
One more step and it all crumbles.

358
26:02.854 --> 26:05.381
That tower that you worked so hard on building.

359
26:05.381 --> 26:06.837
Pardon?

360
26:06.837 --> 26:08.504
There's no use pretending.

361
26:08.504 --> 26:10.773
Your insides are all burnt black.

362
26:10.773 --> 26:12.688
It's just ashes in there.

363
26:12.688 --> 26:14.537
How did you know?

364
26:15.544 --> 26:18.926
And with you, mister...

365
26:28.264 --> 26:30.064
Who are you?

366
26:30.064 --> 26:33.649
Who are you, you fox!

367
26:33.649 --> 26:36.788
Some wretch has taken over your body.

368
26:38.001 --> 26:40.222
Who? Who is it?

369
26:44.123 --> 26:46.656
Oh my, Grandmama...

370
26:46.656 --> 26:48.762
You like it there, don't you!

371
26:48.762 --> 26:50.436
He's young,

372
26:50.436 --> 26:52.142
and handsome...

373
26:52.142 --> 26:55.305
he's a great source of energy.

374
26:55.305 --> 26:56.952
There's no place better, huh?

375
26:56.952 --> 26:58.716
You love it, don't you!

376
27:04.024 --> 27:06.396
Grandmama likes it in you.

377
27:06.396 --> 27:09.792
She looks like she wants to stay.

378
27:09.792 --> 27:11.695
So, an old lady? Who is she?

379
27:11.695 --> 27:16.199
Sis, your troubles are also because this hag is in your twin brother.

380
27:16.199 --> 27:19.661
You're twins, so it takes double the effort.

381
27:19.661 --> 27:21.325
Double...

382
27:21.325 --> 27:23.390
the effort.

383
27:24.705 --> 27:26.249
Well, how much will it cost?

384
27:26.249 --> 27:27.764
10 million won!

385
27:28.887 --> 27:29.888
It's a rip-off.

386
27:29.888 --> 27:31.100
10 million?

387
27:31.100 --> 27:32.393
Yes.

388
27:32.986 --> 27:34.838
Should we ask Mom?

389
27:38.940 --> 27:40.281
Hey.

390
27:45.172 --> 27:46.581
Hey!

391
27:57.753 --> 27:59.238
Kiddo.

392
28:03.139 --> 28:04.639
Is it you?

393
28:05.297 --> 28:08.419
The one who's selling my name to rip people off?

394
28:10.116 --> 28:11.893
You... you're lying.

395
28:13.873 --> 28:15.885
Open your eyes.

396
28:15.885 --> 28:17.412
Grandma?

397
28:17.412 --> 28:19.770
Are... are you actually there?

398
28:23.576 --> 28:27.028
How low can you go, ripping money off of kids?

399
28:27.028 --> 28:28.029
Kiddo.

400
28:28.029 --> 28:30.141
If you keep using that money to satiate your own greed,

401
28:30.141 --> 28:32.359
your guardian spirit will get mad and leave you for good.

402
28:32.359 --> 28:34.647
No use crying about it to me when it happens.

403
28:34.647 --> 28:36.315
No... no way.

404
28:36.315 --> 28:38.306
It's not really her.

405
28:40.892 --> 28:42.852
Which hag are you! Who are you!

406
28:42.852 --> 28:45.170
Stop it with the hag!

407
28:52.598 --> 28:53.944
Hey...

408
28:56.925 --> 28:57.926
Yeah.

409
28:57.926 --> 28:59.669
My grandma says...

410
28:59.669 --> 29:01.526
if you keep calling her a hag,

411
29:01.526 --> 29:05.132
I should rip your tongue out and throw it at the tapestry over there.

412
29:05.132 --> 29:07.645
Do you want to see her angry?

413
29:10.153 --> 29:11.367
Get those hands off the table!

414
29:11.367 --> 29:13.637
I will, I am, I have!

415
29:14.826 --> 29:17.059
I won't, I'm sorry, please! Just leave!

416
29:17.059 --> 29:19.345
Please, leave!

417
29:20.438 --> 29:22.672
Leave!

418
29:22.672 --> 29:24.016
"Spiritual guide," my foot.

419
29:24.016 --> 29:25.259
We're broke high schoolers! 10 million?

420
29:25.259 --> 29:26.437
And out of mom's pockets, no less?

421
29:26.437 --> 29:29.896
Your brain must've gone back in time as well.

422
29:30.876 --> 29:31.900
Have you lost it?

423
29:31.900 --> 29:34.954
Isn't it the effort that counts?

424
29:34.954 --> 29:36.288
If you hit me now,

425
29:36.288 --> 29:38.725
you're just a dude hitting a girl!

426
29:43.009 --> 29:44.972
- Wait up! - Screw off.

427
29:44.972 --> 29:46.328
Why?

428
29:46.328 --> 29:47.544
I said, bugger off!

429
29:47.544 --> 29:49.603
Wait for me!

430
30:10.912 --> 30:12.534
Yoon Ha Na.

431
30:13.404 --> 30:15.203
What?

432
30:16.129 --> 30:18.865
That wasn't very big-brotherly of me to put you under pressure.

433
30:18.865 --> 30:20.365
Sorry.

434
30:21.039 --> 30:22.845
Whatever.

435
30:22.845 --> 30:25.579
I wasn't thinking hard enough.

436
30:25.579 --> 30:26.854
And now I realize

437
30:26.854 --> 30:29.144
that I need to think even less.

438
30:30.623 --> 30:32.070
- What? - See.

439
30:32.070 --> 30:33.700
Let's think simply.

440
30:33.700 --> 30:35.725
The very reason we're here...

441
30:35.725 --> 30:37.232
is Jung Woo Jae.

442
30:37.232 --> 30:39.160
Not my trials.

443
30:39.872 --> 30:41.239
So?

444
30:41.239 --> 30:43.175
Saving Woo Jae comes first.

445
30:43.175 --> 30:45.426
Let's see him make it into the team,

446
30:45.426 --> 30:47.186
and return to the present.

447
30:47.845 --> 30:49.678
What about you?

448
30:49.678 --> 30:50.879
What about it?

449
30:50.879 --> 30:52.404
I've been a judo player my whole life.

450
30:52.404 --> 30:55.391
Missing my shot at this one trial won't spell out the end for me.

451
30:56.929 --> 30:59.166
Oh, come on, it's fine.

452
30:59.166 --> 31:00.742
Go on, go!

453
31:06.931 --> 31:11.476
I'll... do my best.

454
31:11.476 --> 31:13.730
Yoon Ha Ru, your life...

455
31:15.128 --> 31:17.112
I'll protect it as well.

456
31:23.548 --> 31:25.239
- But... - What now?

457
31:25.239 --> 31:27.282
Jung Woo Jae.

458
31:27.282 --> 31:28.648
What do we do with him?

459
31:28.648 --> 31:30.068
Huh?

460
31:30.704 --> 31:32.583
It's fine.

461
31:33.343 --> 31:35.117
It's not fine.

462
31:36.042 --> 31:37.642
It's fine.

463
31:38.315 --> 31:40.415
It's not fine.

464
31:41.355 --> 31:42.955
It's fine...

465
31:47.967 --> 31:49.231
I like you!

466
31:49.231 --> 31:51.642
Huh? What?

467
31:58.231 --> 31:59.820
It's not fine.

468
31:59.820 --> 32:01.681
Not at all.

469
32:01.681 --> 32:04.961
This is driving me nuts!

470
32:21.148 --> 32:22.453
Come on!

471
32:22.453 --> 32:24.615
Alright, I'm going.

472
32:24.615 --> 32:26.091
Don't mess around, okay?

473
32:26.091 --> 32:29.972
I got it, stop treating me like an idiot!

474
32:31.473 --> 32:34.149
- Go on! - I said alright!

475
32:37.609 --> 32:39.154
Yoon Ha Ru!

476
32:41.256 --> 32:43.036
Go, go!

477
33:02.735 --> 33:05.005
Ha Na.

478
33:05.005 --> 33:06.456
Hi.

479
33:19.314 --> 33:20.981
- I... - I...

480
33:25.829 --> 33:27.512
You go first.

481
33:27.512 --> 33:28.738
Okay.

482
33:28.738 --> 33:30.268
Well...

483
33:30.268 --> 33:34.723
About... what you said last night.

484
33:35.364 --> 33:37.215
Oh, that.

485
33:38.101 --> 33:39.541
I must've freaked you out.

486
33:39.541 --> 33:42.261
Yeah, for real, it freaked me...

487
33:45.201 --> 33:48.946
Well, it was a bit surprising, I guess.

488
33:50.063 --> 33:51.423
But...

489
33:52.525 --> 33:54.792
Well, what I meant to say is...

490
33:54.792 --> 33:56.323
I...

491
34:05.784 --> 34:07.432
Thank you.

492
34:08.842 --> 34:09.843
Huh?

493
34:09.843 --> 34:12.182
For feeling that way towards me.

494
34:12.182 --> 34:13.706
Thanks.

495
34:16.508 --> 34:19.536
It's nothing, really.

496
34:21.686 --> 34:24.002
The thing is, though...

497
34:24.002 --> 34:25.502
I, uh...

498
34:29.058 --> 34:30.923
Right now,

499
34:30.923 --> 34:34.231
you're about to face a very important trial.

500
34:34.820 --> 34:38.506
I need to study for my college entrance, too.

501
34:39.269 --> 34:40.409
Yeah.

502
34:40.409 --> 34:42.199
Which is why I think...

503
34:42.199 --> 34:43.708
I get what you mean.

504
34:43.708 --> 34:44.732
Huh?

505
34:44.732 --> 34:45.934
No, wait.

506
34:45.934 --> 34:48.455
- I'm not finished... - You're right, Ha Na.

507
34:49.044 --> 34:51.932
I was being too rash.

508
34:53.031 --> 34:57.891
I wanted to wait until after the trials to properly confess to you.

509
34:58.808 --> 35:00.330
That day was a mistake.

510
35:00.330 --> 35:01.504
Hey, no.

511
35:01.504 --> 35:03.794
Don't call it a mistake.

512
35:05.152 --> 35:07.197
I'll confess to you again, properly...

513
35:07.197 --> 35:09.485
after the trials.

514
35:10.515 --> 35:11.975
When I make the national team,

515
35:11.975 --> 35:14.142
and you get admitted to your dream college...

516
35:14.142 --> 35:16.001
we'll talk again.

517
35:16.001 --> 35:17.888
Oh, yeah.

518
35:17.888 --> 35:19.759
Okay, let's do that.

519
35:19.759 --> 35:21.652
Yeah, I like the sound of that.

520
35:21.652 --> 35:23.462
Thank you for starting this conversation with me.

521
35:23.462 --> 35:24.816
Oh, it's nothing.

522
35:24.816 --> 35:26.424
No need to thank me.

523
35:31.370 --> 35:32.969
That's a relief.

524
35:38.995 --> 35:40.862
It's settled, then.

525
35:40.862 --> 35:42.418
Now...

526
35:42.418 --> 35:44.724
let's just focus on him making it into the team.

527
35:46.355 --> 35:47.952
[National team trials, D-15]

528
36:24.439 --> 36:27.085
[National team trials, D-12]

529
36:51.897 --> 36:54.535
[National team trials, D-5]

530
37:09.626 --> 37:11.519
[National team trials, D-day] This day calls for a barbecue!

531
37:11.519 --> 37:14.316
Not pork, no, it has to be beef.

532
37:22.849 --> 37:24.727
Today's the day.

533
37:25.515 --> 37:26.845
Yeah.

534
37:28.316 --> 37:30.033
Let's give it our best.

535
37:30.033 --> 37:32.179
Yeah, let's do this.

536
37:36.758 --> 37:39.060
- Everyone on board? - Yes, sir!

537
37:41.246 --> 37:43.854
Today's dinner...

538
37:43.854 --> 37:46.741
It's up to you whether I pay for a chicken dinner or a beef banquet!

539
37:46.741 --> 37:48.429
Prove yourselves on the mat, got it?

540
37:48.429 --> 37:49.141
- Yes, sir! - Okay!

541
37:49.141 --> 37:50.779
You heard him, folks!

542
37:50.779 --> 37:52.999
We'll run him bankrupt with a beef banquet!

543
37:52.999 --> 37:54.755
We'll show him what we're made of!

544
37:54.755 --> 37:57.360
- Let's do this! - Let's go!

545
37:57.360 --> 38:02.819
- Beef! Beef! - Beef! Beef!

546
38:03.887 --> 38:07.317
Mom! We need to leave!

547
38:08.500 --> 38:12.273
Your mom always takes so long to get ready to go anywhere ever!

548
38:12.273 --> 38:13.315
Takes a lifetime.

549
38:13.315 --> 38:16.499
Mom! Do you even know what time it is? What if there's traffic?

550
38:16.499 --> 38:18.022
We won't be late.

551
38:18.022 --> 38:19.573
Stop fussing!

552
38:19.573 --> 38:21.259
The trials will last the whole darn day anyway.

553
38:21.259 --> 38:23.240
Well, Ha Ru will only be competing for so long.

554
38:23.240 --> 38:24.419
Come on, come on!

555
38:24.419 --> 38:26.518
- Alright, let's go! - Let's!

556
38:26.518 --> 38:27.692
- We're leaving now! - Let's go!

557
38:27.692 --> 38:29.439
- You've got everything, right? - Yeah!

558
38:29.439 --> 38:31.259
- Okay, let's go! - Go!

559
38:31.259 --> 38:32.744
Oh, wait, wait!

560
38:32.744 --> 38:33.845
What is it now?

561
38:33.845 --> 38:36.026
I forgot something! Wait!

562
38:36.026 --> 38:38.295
You're for sure your mother's daughter!

563
38:38.295 --> 38:40.791
Hush and go get the car ready!

564
39:00.227 --> 39:03.751
Woo Jae, this is the day.

565
39:03.751 --> 39:05.468
After today,

566
39:05.468 --> 39:07.668
things will be different.

567
39:22.884 --> 39:26.454
I'll end our days of pain and anguish.

568
39:27.097 --> 39:29.400
I will make sure of it.

569
39:38.897 --> 39:41.190
You think Ha Ru will do well?

570
39:41.190 --> 39:42.918
Of course.

571
39:42.918 --> 39:44.155
But honey, have you noticed?

572
39:44.155 --> 39:47.125
The tension today is way stronger.

573
39:47.125 --> 39:49.025
Yes, but I don't see why.

574
39:49.025 --> 39:51.533
This isn't the first time Ha Ru has competed.

575
39:51.533 --> 39:55.051
Don't you worry, Madam Jung Yeong Sook.

576
39:59.904 --> 40:02.385
Don't forget to bring this tomorrow.

577
40:02.385 --> 40:03.885
Yeah.

578
40:05.154 --> 40:09.252
We'll be able to make it back tomorrow, right?

579
40:09.975 --> 40:11.953
We will.

580
40:11.953 --> 40:14.599
Woo Jae will make it in, no matter what.

581
40:17.692 --> 40:18.878
And me, as well...

582
40:18.878 --> 40:19.879
No,

583
40:19.879 --> 40:21.379
I mean, you...

584
40:21.379 --> 40:23.507
will make it, too.

585
40:23.507 --> 40:25.688
I'll try my absolute best.

586
40:25.688 --> 40:26.920
Don't exert yourself.

587
40:26.920 --> 40:28.989
Just don't get hurt.

588
40:29.842 --> 40:31.226
Okay.

589
40:34.341 --> 40:36.848
Ha Ru takes after me, he'll do fine.

590
40:36.848 --> 40:39.862
Please make it in, Ha Ru...

591
40:39.862 --> 40:41.956
Oh, please, please...

592
40:41.956 --> 40:44.134
Are you even listening to me?

593
40:46.218 --> 40:47.532
[Shinil Sports Complex]

594
40:47.532 --> 40:49.755
Let's do this!

595
40:50.443 --> 40:51.959
Look at the thug.

596
40:51.959 --> 40:53.518
He's gotten even more buff!

597
40:53.518 --> 40:54.978
That's scary.

598
40:54.978 --> 40:55.979
- You scared? - Yeah...

599
40:55.979 --> 40:57.039
That's cute.

600
40:57.039 --> 40:58.089
He's going to cry today.

601
40:58.089 --> 40:59.761
Hey, look at him.

602
41:02.767 --> 41:04.604
Well, well.

603
41:04.604 --> 41:06.279
Look who it is.

604
41:10.446 --> 41:13.146
I thought you quit judo. Crawling back like a dog?

605
41:13.146 --> 41:14.717
Have you no shame?

606
41:15.825 --> 41:17.317
Why's that?

607
41:17.317 --> 41:19.537
Did you realize once you left the judo scene

608
41:19.537 --> 41:21.737
that you're no good for anything else?

609
41:28.309 --> 41:29.938
See you later.

610
41:36.695 --> 41:38.913
What's his problem?

611
41:39.910 --> 41:41.928
Are you okay?

612
41:42.788 --> 41:43.979
Yeah.

613
41:46.470 --> 41:47.702
Who the hell is he?

614
41:47.702 --> 41:50.215
Baekyeon High School's judo thug?

615
41:50.215 --> 41:51.216
A chick?

616
41:51.216 --> 41:53.177
That's Lee Hyeong Won.

617
41:54.769 --> 41:56.579
Lee Hyeong Won?

618
41:59.442 --> 42:00.987
Let's go.

619
42:02.332 --> 42:03.635
Okay.

620
42:14.598 --> 42:16.044
Everyone!

621
42:18.624 --> 42:20.702
You are all nameless on the mat.

622
42:20.702 --> 42:22.884
Either you are a winner or a loser.

623
42:22.884 --> 42:24.232
You'll climb off that mat with either of those names.

624
42:24.232 --> 42:25.311
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

625
42:25.311 --> 42:27.432
I'll make it short. Just remember three things.

626
42:27.432 --> 42:30.380
Don't let go of the collar, keep eye contact,

627
42:30.380 --> 42:32.663
and... endure. Whatever it takes.

628
42:32.663 --> 42:33.629
Understood?

629
42:33.629 --> 42:35.569
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

630
42:36.201 --> 42:37.412
Today...

631
42:37.412 --> 42:39.843
we'll have that beef banquet!

632
42:46.281 --> 42:47.870
Good luck.

633
43:06.775 --> 43:08.352
There he is!

634
43:20.745 --> 43:21.658
Go, Yoon Ha Ru!

635
43:21.658 --> 43:23.718
- Show them! - Go, Yoon Ha Ru!

636
43:32.538 --> 43:33.977
Start!

637
43:43.893 --> 43:46.245
[National team trials, round of 16] [Lee Hyeong Won : Pyo Gyeong Woo]

638
44:01.537 --> 44:03.778
Yes, that's it! Tear him apart!

639
44:21.389 --> 44:22.674
[Lee Hyeong Won]

640
44:23.552 --> 44:26.695
The judo thug, Lee Hyeong Won!

641
44:26.695 --> 44:29.988
He was talented, but he dropped off the face of the earth one day.

642
44:30.865 --> 44:33.247
I wonder what he's doing now.

643
44:35.689 --> 44:36.994
[Jung Woo Jae : Kim Dong Gil]

644
44:39.064 --> 44:40.580
Go!

645
44:43.439 --> 44:44.644
Start!

646
44:52.714 --> 44:54.077
Good!

647
44:54.706 --> 44:57.071
That's it, Jung Woo Jae!

648
45:03.355 --> 45:04.499
[Yoon Ha Ru : Jang Won]

649
45:10.355 --> 45:11.637
Start!

650
45:23.274 --> 45:26.076
Yes, defend! Defense position, there you go!

651
45:34.373 --> 45:35.794
Stop!

652
45:37.818 --> 45:40.546
- It's okay! - Thank goodness!

653
45:41.391 --> 45:43.591
Go, Ha Ru!

654
45:46.573 --> 45:48.638
Yoon Ha Ru!

655
45:48.638 --> 45:49.639
Don't give up!

656
45:49.639 --> 45:50.914
Don't give up yet!

657
45:50.914 --> 45:53.669
Don't you dare give up!

658
45:53.669 --> 45:55.169
Let's go!

659
46:01.158 --> 46:02.373
Start!

660
46:06.549 --> 46:09.384
- Go, go, Yoon Ha Ru! - Go!

661
46:09.384 --> 46:11.204
Go, go!

662
46:11.204 --> 46:13.404
You're doing great!

663
46:20.699 --> 46:22.617
- Full point! - Let's go!

664
46:24.929 --> 46:26.430
Stop!

665
46:26.430 --> 46:31.813
- Yoon Ha Ru! - Yoon Ha Ru!

666
46:34.355 --> 46:36.315
[National team trials, round of 8] [Jung Woo Jae : Park Sung Soo]

667
46:41.788 --> 46:43.389
Pinning!

668
46:49.830 --> 46:51.249
Half point!

669
46:51.917 --> 46:53.342
Full point!

670
47:02.856 --> 47:04.394
[Round of 8] [Yoon Ha Ru : Lee Hyeong Won]

671
47:11.411 --> 47:14.445
You dare hit Woo Jae's shoulder?

672
47:14.445 --> 47:15.498
You bastard...

673
47:15.498 --> 47:17.402
You're dead.

674
47:29.952 --> 47:31.289
Start!

675
47:38.195 --> 47:39.624
I can do this!

676
47:39.624 --> 47:41.750
Yoon Ha Ru won all of these matches anyway.

677
47:41.750 --> 47:42.847
I can do this!

678
47:42.847 --> 47:44.748
I can protect everyone...

679
47:52.060 --> 47:53.569
Are you okay?

680
47:55.102 --> 47:56.726
Go, go!

681
48:05.741 --> 48:07.106
Yoon Ha Na.

682
48:07.106 --> 48:08.785
You can do it!

683
48:08.785 --> 48:10.110
Start!

684
48:22.496 --> 48:24.760
Wait, that's...

685
48:32.754 --> 48:34.170
Full point!

686
48:42.013 --> 48:43.910
That's it, Yoon Ha Na.

687
48:50.929 --> 48:52.488
See it through, Ha Na.

688
48:52.488 --> 48:54.011
Please...

689
48:56.663 --> 48:58.390
No, Yoon Ha Na...

690
48:58.390 --> 49:00.347
Do it for Ha Ru!

691
49:00.347 --> 49:02.255
Don't!

692
49:02.255 --> 49:03.928
Come on!

693
49:28.522 --> 49:29.862
What's going on?

694
49:33.603 --> 49:35.601
It'll be okay.

695
49:36.452 --> 49:39.132
- Go! Check on him! - Oh, wait...

696
49:46.306 --> 49:48.059
You'll have to go see a doctor.

697
49:48.059 --> 49:49.428
Get some tests done.

698
49:49.428 --> 49:51.639
Oh, no, my baby...

699
49:51.639 --> 49:53.094
It'll be alright.

700
49:53.094 --> 49:54.735
It's no big deal.

701
49:58.147 --> 50:00.134
[Round of 4] [Jung Woo Jae : Lee Hyeong Won]

702
50:19.564 --> 50:20.838
Start!

703
50:28.085 --> 50:29.883
Oh, right.

704
50:29.883 --> 50:31.795
Woo Jae's semifinal will start soon...

705
50:31.795 --> 50:34.189
Oh, I'll go keep watch.

706
50:37.280 --> 50:39.683
- Another ice pack, please. - Alright.

707
50:49.526 --> 50:53.269
- Beef banquet! - Beef, beef, beef!

708
51:34.299 --> 51:35.549
What?

709
51:35.549 --> 51:36.573
Lee Hyeong Won...

710
51:36.573 --> 51:39.400
This is how he disappeared?

711
51:49.775 --> 51:51.494
Hey, Lee Hyeong Won!

712
51:52.652 --> 51:54.328
Where are you going?

713
51:56.410 --> 51:58.858
- What's it to you? - I asked you a question.

714
51:58.858 --> 52:00.401
Get lost.

715
52:00.401 --> 52:01.750
Why?

716
52:01.750 --> 52:04.690
Are you giving up because of one lost match?

717
52:08.002 --> 52:09.487
Shut it.

718
52:09.487 --> 52:11.055
I'll still punch a girl.

719
52:11.055 --> 52:12.279
It's not over for you yet.

720
52:12.279 --> 52:13.887
There's a repechage, you know.

721
52:13.887 --> 52:15.866
You can secure a bronze medal if you're lucky.

722
52:15.866 --> 52:17.407
A bronze?

723
52:17.407 --> 52:19.174
What good is that?

724
52:19.174 --> 52:20.749
Who's going to acknowledge me for a 3rd place?

725
52:20.749 --> 52:22.329
Are you that out of touch?

726
52:22.329 --> 52:23.845
What's wrong with coming in 3rd place?

727
52:23.845 --> 52:25.371
It's better than running away without even trying.

728
52:25.371 --> 52:28.045
Way cooler than the pathetic rat you're acting like right now.

729
52:28.045 --> 52:30.324
It's not even worth the comparison, really.

730
52:31.289 --> 52:32.825
What did you just say?

731
52:35.399 --> 52:38.222
Hey, hey! The repechage, it's...

732
52:40.098 --> 52:42.032
- Uh, I... - No way.

733
52:42.032 --> 52:43.692
We need to go see a doctor.

734
52:43.692 --> 52:44.936
Let's go.

735
52:44.936 --> 52:46.103
No, but...

736
52:46.103 --> 52:48.154
- But I... - Ha Ru.

737
52:49.209 --> 52:50.788
Let's go to the hospital.

738
52:58.301 --> 52:59.695
Get back in there.

739
52:59.695 --> 53:02.680
You still have a chance at this.

740
53:02.680 --> 53:03.892
Choose.

741
53:03.892 --> 53:06.200
Do you want to be a judo player,

742
53:06.200 --> 53:08.264
or end up a miserable twat?

743
53:24.647 --> 53:26.446
[Baekyeon High School]

744
53:58.538 --> 54:00.055
I'm sorry.

745
54:01.511 --> 54:03.990
You told me not to get injured,

746
54:05.048 --> 54:07.248
but I couldn't even manage that.

747
54:08.522 --> 54:09.772
What are you on about?

748
54:09.772 --> 54:10.995
Don't tell me...

749
54:10.995 --> 54:13.355
You're conscious of me? That's so not you.

750
54:14.530 --> 54:16.730
I wanted to...

751
54:17.795 --> 54:20.340
protect your life as well, you know.

752
54:21.771 --> 54:23.417
Are you crying?

753
54:25.109 --> 54:29.442
How did you manage to memorize all those lines as an actress with your empty noggin?

754
54:30.919 --> 54:33.703
- What? - We came here for one reason.

755
54:33.703 --> 54:35.667
Don't tell me you forgot it already.

756
54:35.667 --> 54:36.953
Jung Woo Jae.

757
54:36.953 --> 54:40.681
Not my trials. Jung Woo Jae, got it?

758
54:40.681 --> 54:42.623
Idiot.

759
54:46.128 --> 54:48.977
We saw him make it into the team.

760
54:48.977 --> 54:50.773
Our work is over here.

761
54:51.884 --> 54:55.514
I'll save my own skin. Don't make a big deal out of it.

762
54:57.147 --> 54:59.421
Well, now, let's go back!

763
55:01.162 --> 55:03.825
- But... - What now?

764
55:03.825 --> 55:05.898
We don't know how to.

765
55:05.898 --> 55:07.329
Not yet.

766
55:07.329 --> 55:08.943
Damn, you're right.

767
55:17.965 --> 55:19.480
That didn't work.

768
55:20.566 --> 55:23.952
I guess just dropping it isn't what triggers it.

769
55:25.304 --> 55:26.839
Well, let's try whatever we can.

770
55:26.839 --> 55:29.039
If it wants a fight, we'll give it a fight.

771
55:34.814 --> 55:36.938
Huh? What's up with the weather?

772
55:36.938 --> 55:38.872
Hey, are you alright?

773
55:38.872 --> 55:40.184
I'm fine.

774
55:46.788 --> 55:47.922
Huh?

775
55:47.922 --> 55:49.350
What the...

776
55:49.350 --> 55:51.777
My alumna, Shin Bi Gyeong?

777
55:51.777 --> 55:54.239
Hello, it's 2013.

778
55:54.239 --> 55:57.458
This is the after-party for Yongwon University's Department of Film!

779
55:57.458 --> 55:59.822
Coming to you live!

780
55:59.822 --> 56:02.392
- Applaud! - 2013?

781
56:02.392 --> 56:05.626
Did the rain trigger another time leap?

782
56:05.626 --> 56:10.148
Our alumni are getting blackout drunk right now, as we speak!

783
56:10.148 --> 56:12.024
Let's see for ourselves.

784
56:12.024 --> 56:13.567
- Chug, chug, chug! - Ye Rang!

785
56:13.567 --> 56:16.010
- Film is life! - Right, around this time, I assumed

786
56:16.010 --> 56:17.941
- she'd become an actress. - And life is a long take!

787
56:17.941 --> 56:21.857
- And Jun Mo... He looks so young looking back. - Chug it, chug!

788
56:21.857 --> 56:24.901
Han Soo Hyuk is... well, Han Soo Hyuk.

789
56:24.901 --> 56:27.569
Let's hand it over to reporter Yoon Ha Na.

790
56:27.569 --> 56:30.339
Here you go, reporter Yoon Ha Na...

791
56:30.966 --> 56:34.929
Did you just call me Yoon Ha Na?

792
56:36.019 --> 56:38.117
Huh? It's me!

793
56:38.117 --> 56:40.092
It's Yoon Ha Na!

794
56:43.682 --> 56:45.430
But why 2013?

795
56:45.430 --> 56:48.472
Why not 2026? Why is it 2013?

796
56:48.472 --> 56:50.103
What's wrong, Ha Na?

797
56:50.103 --> 56:51.188
You alright, Ha Na?

798
56:51.188 --> 56:53.376
I'd be 21 in 2013...

799
56:53.376 --> 56:55.080
So, if he's 21...

800
56:55.080 --> 56:57.700
Woo Jae must be serving in the army.

801
57:00.826 --> 57:02.515
- Hey, where are you going? - Yoon Ha Na!

802
57:02.515 --> 57:04.129
Where are you going?

803
57:06.076 --> 57:07.989
Why is this happening?

804
57:07.989 --> 57:10.300
What went wrong?

805
57:10.300 --> 57:13.727
[Beast] Why won't he answer?

806
57:16.132 --> 57:17.626
Oh, my purse!

807
57:17.626 --> 57:18.736
Thief!

808
57:18.736 --> 57:21.368
- Move! - It's a thief! A thief!

809
57:23.632 --> 57:24.845
Move!

810
57:24.845 --> 57:27.071
- He's a thief! - Out of the way!

811
57:28.564 --> 57:30.247
You're not going anywhere!

812
57:31.791 --> 57:33.122
Piss off!

813
57:38.397 --> 57:39.933
Let go!

814
57:42.937 --> 57:43.938
Are you alright?

815
57:43.938 --> 57:45.611
Woo Jae!

816
57:51.982 --> 57:53.707
Are you hurt?

817
57:55.864 --> 57:57.471
You scum!

818
57:57.471 --> 57:58.971
Stay down!

819
58:10.984 --> 58:12.906
Oh, thank you.

820
58:25.341 --> 58:26.690
Ha Na.

821
58:26.690 --> 58:28.242
You sure you're okay?

822
58:28.242 --> 58:31.524
Oh, yeah, I'm totally fine.

823
58:32.155 --> 58:35.149
Are you sure you're okay?

824
58:35.149 --> 58:36.702
Of course I'm fine.

825
58:36.702 --> 58:38.381
I got your purse back, didn't I?

826
58:38.381 --> 58:40.679
No, I mean, you...

827
58:41.307 --> 58:42.418
Where do you live now?

828
58:42.418 --> 58:44.065
What about judo?

829
58:46.256 --> 58:48.993
Are you that drunk, Ha Na?

830
58:52.548 --> 58:54.071
I...

831
58:54.071 --> 58:55.943
I quit, remember?

832
58:56.683 --> 58:58.909
- Judo... - What? Why?

833
58:58.909 --> 59:02.183
But you were first place in the national trial! Why would you quit judo?

834
59:02.183 --> 59:03.683
I mean, why did you?

835
59:20.296 --> 59:21.903
Everyone's drinking a lot.

836
59:21.903 --> 59:23.809
I guess it's fair, being the after-party of our campus festival.

837
59:23.809 --> 59:25.755
Our department seemed like they wouldn't stop drinking, too.

838
59:25.755 --> 59:27.873
So I left after I got some dinner in me.

839
59:27.873 --> 59:29.598
- Your department? - Yeah.

840
59:29.598 --> 59:32.847
By the way, we have a whopping three new female students.

841
59:32.847 --> 59:35.355
Becoming a bodyguard was their childhood dream.

842
59:35.355 --> 59:36.843
How cool is that?

843
59:37.584 --> 59:39.213
Bodyguard?

844
59:42.074 --> 59:43.526
Yeah.

845
59:52.944 --> 59:54.235
[Beast]

846
59:54.950 --> 59:56.451
Just a moment.

847
59:56.451 --> 59:57.753
Okay.

848
59:59.451 --> 01:00:01.541
What took you so long?

849
01:00:01.541 --> 01:00:03.735
[Yoon's Raw Fish Restaurant] Yoon Ha Ru, where are you right now?

850
01:00:04.700 --> 01:00:06.239
- Yoon Ha Na. - Yeah?

851
01:00:06.239 --> 01:00:08.295
Where the hell are you?

852
01:00:08.295 --> 01:00:09.367
Haesol.

853
01:00:09.367 --> 01:00:10.473
Haesol?

854
01:00:10.473 --> 01:00:11.633
What are you doing there?

855
01:00:11.633 --> 01:00:13.508
Working part-time at our parents' restaurant.

856
01:00:13.508 --> 01:00:15.490
I'm not a judo player.

857
01:00:16.812 --> 01:00:20.504
I gave up... on judo.

858
01:00:22.144 --> 01:00:23.488
What?

859
01:00:57.968 --> 01:01:00.202
Nothing's going as we expected.

860
01:01:00.202 --> 01:01:04.735
Everyone was worried about the two idiots who knew nothing other than judo.

861
01:01:04.735 --> 01:01:06.679
How do I even do this?

862
01:01:06.679 --> 01:01:07.918
Chef.

863
01:01:07.918 --> 01:01:10.622
Why choose to be a bodyguard?

864
01:01:10.622 --> 01:01:12.722
I have someone I want to protect.

865
01:01:12.722 --> 01:01:14.266
[That Summer, Us: Male Actor Audition] What if...

866
01:01:14.266 --> 01:01:16.657
that someone became the protector?

867
01:01:16.657 --> 01:01:18.061
[We will protect Jung Woo Jae!] Ta-da!

868
01:01:18.061 --> 01:01:19.435
Woo Jae...

869
01:01:19.435 --> 01:01:20.833
I'm going to make him an actor.

870
01:01:20.833 --> 01:01:23.423
Physically adept, action-ready, and a killer gaze. That's you!

871
01:01:23.423 --> 01:01:25.847
- Me? - You'll be Jung Woo Jae, worldwide star!

872
01:01:25.847 --> 01:01:30.382
Turns out, it wasn't just the medal that I wanted to take from you.

873
01:01:30.382 --> 01:01:32.635
If you can't put faith in yourself,

874
01:01:32.635 --> 01:01:35.011
put faith in me, who believes in you.
